          ],
          "INC-SOURCE": [
            {
              "pointer": "",
              "coded_information": {
                "incident_source": [
                  "SPALL"
                ],
                "reaction": null
              },
              "free_text": [
                " Spallation reaction in a mercury target",
                "irradiated with 3-GeV protons.",
                "The proton beam was supplied at a repetition rate",
                "of 25 Hz and in the \"double-bunch mode\", in which",
                "the pulsed protons consist of two bunches, each with",
                "a width of 100 ns, at intervals of 600 ns.",
                "To improve neutron energy resolution, a Si neutron",
                "filter with thickness of 20 cm were installed."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "METHOD": [
            {
              "pointer": "",
              "coded_information": [
                "FNB",
                "TOF",
                "PHWT"
              ],
              "free_text": [
                "",
                "Neutron TOF experiment with a neutron filtering system.",
                "The neutron capture yield was derived by applying the",
                "pulse-height weighting technique (PHWT)."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "INC-SPECT": [
            {
              "pointer": "",
              "coded_information": [
                "EN-RSL"
              ],
              "free_text": [
                " One standard deviation.",
                "Filtered neutron spectra for 51.5 and 127.7 keV are",
                "given in REL-REF (NIM/A,1003,165318,2021)."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "DETECTOR": [
            {
              "pointer": "",
              "coded_information": [
                "NAICR"
              ],
              "free_text": [
                "",
                " -Size: 330 mm (diam.) and 203 mm in thickness",
                " -Angle: 90 deg with respect to the neutron beam line",
                " -Flight length: 27.9 m",
                " -DAQ: CAEN V1720 Digitizer (12bit, 250MHz)"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "SAMPLE": [
            {
              "pointer": "",
              "coded_information": null,
              "free_text": [
                "129I sample:",
                "  A NaI pellet with a mass of 404 +- 1 mg and",
                "  activity of 2.65 MBq, sealed in a Ti case.",
                "  The sample contained 129I with a abundance of 85.9%,",
                "  together with 14.1% of 127I as an impurity.",
                "  Area density: 127I (1.13 +- 0.03) x10E-4 at/b",
                "                129I (6.83 +- 0.07) x10E-4 at/b",
                "127I Sample:",
                "  A nat-NaI compressed pellet with mass of 562 +- 1 mg.",
                "  Area density: 127I (7.42 +- 0.07 ) x10E-4 at/b",
                "Dummy sample:",
                "  A replica dummy sample, with the same Ti case and a",
                "  nat-NaI pellet, was measured to derive the background",
                "  events induced by the Ti casing and NaI pellet.",
                "  Area density: 127I (7.21 +- 0.07 ) x10E-4 at/b",
                "Au sample:",
                "  A 197Au sample was employed to normalize the",
                "  cross-section results.",
                "  Area density: natAu (5.93 +- 0.06 ) x10E-4 at/b",
                "Carbon sample:",
                "  A carbon sample was used as neutron scatterer to",
                "  estimate background.",
                "  Area density: natC (8.65 +- 0.09 ) x10E-3 at/b"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "ANALYSIS": [
            {
              "pointer": "",
              "coded_information": null,
              "free_text": [
                "The pulse height weighting technique (PHWT) with the",
                "threshold of 600 keV was applied to derive the neutron",
                "capture yield.",
                "Measurements with the carbon sample, \"Dummy sample\",",
                "and \"Blank (no sample) \" were used for background",
                "estimation. A measurement with the gold sample was",
                "used for the normalization.",
                "The neutron capture cross section was determined",
                "relative to the capture cross section of Au-197.",
                "The neutron capture cross-section of 127I was first",
                "calculated using the 127I sample to then remove its",
                "influence in the 129I cross-section measurement."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "CORRECTION": [
            {
              "pointer": "",
              "coded_information": null,
              "free_text": [
                "Dead time correction was applied with the",
                "non-paralyzable model with a deadtime constant of",
                "1.25 +- 0.01 us.",
                "Correction factors for self shielding and multiple",
                "scattering were deduced using the PHITS."
              ]
            }
          ],
